::ingredients

(juice choice) = (cassis juice, Johannesbeer) 300ml -OR- (juice, another kind) 300ml
(red wine) 1 bottle / 700ml
(sugar) 50g
(raisins) 25g
(orange) 1
(cinnamon bark) 1
(ginger choice) = (ginger, powdered) 1 spoon -OR- (ginger, fresh) a bit
(cloves) 1 spoon
(star anise) 5

::equipment

(pot)

::instructions

(orange) <cut, into nice-looking pieces> # Mainly decoration.
{mulled wine} = (juice choice) + (red wine) + (sugar) + (raisins) + (orange) + (cinnamon bark) + (ginger choice) + (cloves) + (star anise)
    <warm, in (pot), do not boil>
    <enjoy>

::notes

If you cannot find cassis juice, use another juice; the author has used cranberry pomegranate juice.
The author prefers Primitivo/Zinfandel red wine, not cheap cooking wine: you want to drink it :)
If you do not have the spices, use sweet cinnamon tea bags or similar instead; they contain most spices. The author used 6 teabags for 1 litre.

::story

A recipe for Glühwein/mulled wine a beverage you can find at almost every European christmas market. This recipe is my favorite one - optimized for flavor rather than alcohol content (it still kicks in).

